+ * says that the block of this page of the file has not been authenticated yet (any lock that keeps the vnode's
+ * signatures, such as the lock of its VM object, is enough; it never sleeps). cs_native4k_lazy_authenticate does it for
+ * the blocks of a range of the file: it pages the blocks in, so the caller holds no VM lock and no busy page, and keeps
+ * the vnode's signatures alive (a paging reference on its VM object, or a reference on the vnode). It returns
+ * KERN_SUCCESS when every block now has an answer, right or wrong, KERN_RESOURCE_SHORTAGE to wait for memory and try
+ * again, anything else when a block could not be read. vm_fault_cs_lazy_fetch (osfmk/vm/vm_fault.c) copies one page of
+ * the vnode's VM object out for it; cluster_start and cluster_end bound the read around it. vm_fault_cs_lazy_alias is
+ * the writable address, valid to the end of its page, of a byte of the recorded answers, which are mapped read-only.
